nio: call bsdinit_task directly to reach launchd

The checkpoints of run 595 are decisive: the boot reaches
"CHK after utaskbootstrap" but never "CHK before load_init".
The code between them is a short sequence with no blocking call.

The missing step is the handoff to the init process.
bsdinit_task(), which calls load_init_program() and execs
/sbin/launchd, is normally invoked from bsd_ast() the first time
the newly-cloned init thread takes an AST (bsd_init_done == 0
in kern_sig.c).  That thread is never scheduled this early on
this board, so the trigger never fires and the boot stops with
the root mounted and no init.

Call bsdinit_task() directly at the end of bsd_init() instead.
load_init_program() execs launchd, which replaces this thread
with the init process.  A direct-to-framebuffer mark says when
the call is made, so the next photograph shows how far the exec
path gets.  Add the forward declaration; this trimmed tree does
not carry the one from systm.h.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index 97d3784..961ad9e 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -329,6 +329,8 @@ static void process_name(const char *, proc_t);
 
 static void setconf(void);
 
+void bsdinit_task(void);
+
 #if CONFIG_BASESYSTEMROOT
 static int bsd_find_basesystem_dmg(char *bsdmgpath_out, bool *rooted_dmg, bool *skip_signature_check);
 static boolean_t bsdmgroot_bootable(void);
@@ -1269,6 +1271,14 @@ bsd_init(void)
 #endif /* DEVELOPMENT || DEBUG */
 
 	bsd_init_kprintf("done\n");
+	/* nio: bsdinit_task(), which execs /sbin/launchd, is normally reached
+	 * from bsd_ast() the first time the newly-cloned init thread takes an
+	 * AST.  That thread never gets scheduled this early on this board, so
+	 * the trigger never fires and the boot stops here with the root already
+	 * mounted.  Call it directly on this thread instead: load_init_program
+	 * execs launchd, which turns this thread into the init process. */
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: call bsdinit_task directly");
+	bsdinit_task();
 }
 
 #if defined(XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT) && XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT
